Hi Ravi,

Are you using the 1000G calculated LD scores to run LD-score regression (ldsc function in Genomic SEM) or the newer Stratified LDSC feature(s_ldsc function in Genomic SEM)? If you are using the LD scores for traditional LDSC you should be using the file "eur_w_ld_chr" available through the same link you listed or through the Genomic SEM box folder at: https://utexas.app.box.com/s/vkd36n197m8klbaio3yzoxsee6sxo11v

If you are running s_ldsc I would recommend using  1000G_Phase3_baselineLD_v2.2_ldscores.tgz <https://storage.googleapis.com/broad-alkesgroup-public/LDSCORE/1000G_Phase3_baselineLD_v2.2_ldscores.tgz> as some of the earlier baseline versions (such as the v1.2 version you downloaded) the group provides can provide underestimates of total population heritability based on some internal simulations we've performed and reflect the most up-to-date versions recommended by the group at the Broad. Of course let us know if you are still running into error messages or issues.

Best,
  Andrew

